a pytorch server proc will start a tcp-daemon and then connect to it by address:port
recently, we have this case, launch the pytorch in two nodes (n1:192.x.x.0, n2:192.x.x.1), and due to the proc of pytorch is randomly scheduled to a node by the scheduler, so we can't simply assume the server proc is running at n1 or n2
to clarify
n1: the worker proc is running, but server_addr is n1
n2: the server proc is running, but server_addr is n1
server proc and worker proc will timeout after 300s left
though this problem can be solved by the node index, as we can force the server proc running at the index 1 of the node rather then other node
but i propose to add some protected codes or logs around L301 - L310
